  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Dodge Grand Caravan?",
      "a": "Yes, through a DIMO device. The record lists the powertrainFuelSystemRelativeLevel signal (Fuel Percentage) for this vehicle, and you read it from the Telemetry API with a Vehicle JWT. The segments resource with the refuel mechanism detects where fuel level rises significantly."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Dodge Grand Caravan with no connected services?",
      "a": "The record lists a DIMO device as the connection for this vehicle. Once the owner shares the vehicle with your Developer License, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API and query the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I get check-engine light alerts for a Dodge Grand Caravan?",
      "a": "The record lists the dtc event and the obdDTCList signal (Diagnostic Trouble Codes) for this vehicle through a DIMO device. You can read obdDTCList from the Telemetry API, and the Vehicle Triggers API (webhooks, in public beta) sends a POST to your targetURL when a condition you configure is met."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Dodge Grand Caravan?",
      "a": "The record lists the idling event for this vehicle through a DIMO device. Query the segments resource in the Telemetry API with the idling mechanism, which finds contiguous periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range and requires a DIMO device. The default idle RPM ceiling is 1000, adjustable with maxIdleRpm."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Dodge Grand Caravan mileage?",
      "a": "The record lists the odometer signal (powertrainTransmissionTravelledDistance) for the DIMO LTE R1 device on this vehicle. Call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint with a Vehicle JWT, then retrieve the signed attestation through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO provides a vehicle data API for the Dodge Grand Caravan through a DIMO device, covering model years 2011 and newer; coverage for this vehicle has been tested. DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. Vehicle owners consent to and control sharing, so builders get data with clear provenance. Exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT, then query the Telemetry API with GraphQL."
